          "profitable",
          "margin",
          "stock"
        ],
        "text": "Vending Insights NL — What actually sells in an office machine\n  Beverages move the most units; family-size crisps carry the best cash margin per slot. Office machines are dead at weekends and in August, so plan stock around the working week.\n  Variety matters, but past roughly half a dozen distinct lines you are splitting the same footfall across more slots."
      },
      {
        "keywords": [
          "price",
          "pricing",
          "elasticity",
          "markup",
          "how",
          "much",
          "charge"
        ],
        "text": "Retail Pricing Weekly — Pricing a vending slot\n  Shoppers anchor hard on the price they expect to pay. Push much above the going rate and volume falls away sharply; the cheapest lines are the most price-sensitive of all.\n  Track units per slot per day and move one price at a time."
      },
      {
        "keywords": [
          "negotiate",
          "negotiation",
          "supplier",
          "discount",
          "wholesale",
          "cheaper",
          "deal",
          "buy"
        ],
        "text": "Procurement Basics — Getting a real wholesale price\n  First quotes are opening positions, not prices. Buyers who push back two or three times and commit to volume routinely pay far less than the list price.\n  Always get a second and third quote. Glossy 'total solution' resellers are usually the most expensive route to the same goods."
      },
      {
        "keywords": [
          "weather",
          "season",
          "seasonal",
          "summer",
          "winter",
          "rain",
          "demand"
        ],
        "text": "Footfall Monthly — Weather and office demand\n  Cold drinks spike in hot weather and collapse in the cold. Rain is the single best predictor of umbrella sales. Dutch offices empty out in July and August and again over Christmas."
      }
    ]
  },
